{"name":"Steel Toe","hex":"#929894","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artificial metal produced from iron, harder and more elastic than elemental iron; used figuratively as a symbol of hardness.","Any item made of this metal, particularly including:\nBladed or pointed weapons, as swords, javelins, daggers."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of steel.","Similar to steel in color, strength, or the like; steely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steel"},{"term":"toe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["Former ISO 639-3 language code for Tomedes."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Each of the five digits on the end of the human foot.\n\nThe equivalent part in an animal.","The equivalent part in an animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toe"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of Kim Possible characters","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of characters appearing in the animated series Kim Possible and related media."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e6/Kim_Possible_Cast.jpg/330px-Kim_Possible_Cast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Kim_Possible_characters"},{"title":"Steel-toe boot","blocks":[{"text":"A steel-toe boot is a durable boot or shoe that has a protective reinforcement in the toe which protects the foot from falling objects or compression. Safety shoes are effective in keeping the feet of industrial workers safe from sharp and heavy objects while working in factories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Steel-toe_boots.jpg/330px-Steel-toe_boots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel-toe_boot"},{"title":"Steel","blocks":[{"text":"Steel is an alloy of iron and carbon that demonstrates improved mechanical properties compared to the pure form of iron. Due to its high elastic modulus, yield strength, fracture strength and low raw material cost, steel is one of the most commonly manufactured materials in the world. Steel is used in structures, in bridges, infrastructure, tools, ships, trains, cars, bicycles, machines, electrical appliances, furniture, and weapons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel"},{"title":"Toe","blocks":[{"text":"Toes are the digits of the foot of a tetrapod. Animal species such as cats that walk on their toes are described as being digitigrade. Humans, and other animals that walk on the soles of their feet, are described as being plantigrade; unguligrade animals are those that walk on hooves at the tips of their toes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Toes.png/330px-Toes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/S3_safety_footwear.jpg/500px-S3_safety_footwear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/S3_safety_footwear.jpg/1280px-S3_safety_footwear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/S3_safety_footwear.jpg/500px-S3_safety_footwear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of ISO 20345:2004 compliant S3 safety boots","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS3_safety_footwear.jpg"},{"srcs